-- title:
--   Differentials of functions regular at v are regular
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, let $K$ have characteristic zero, and let $x \in F$ be such that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x)$ generated by $x$. Let $v$ be a place of $F$ over $K$, that is, a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ itself, and a principal ideal ring; for $g \in F$ write $\operatorname{ord}_v(g)$ for minus the logarithm of the associated height-one-spectrum adic valuation of $g$. Let $f \in F$ satisfy $\operatorname{ord}_v(f) \ge 0$. Then $0 \le \operatorname{ord}_v$ of the differential $D_{K/F}f$, where the order of a differential $\omega \in \Omega[F/K]$ at $v$ is defined as $\operatorname{ord}_v$ of its coefficient relative to a chosen element $t$ of valuation $1$, namely of the element $g$ chosen with $\omega = g \cdot D_{K/F}t$ (and $0$ if no such $g$ exists). Here $D_{K/F}$ is the universal derivation into the module of Kähler differentials.
--
--   This is the local regularity half of the theory of orders of differentials on a function field of one variable in characteristic zero: a function regular at a place has regular differential there. It is used in the treatment of coefficient maps for modular curves, where differentials attached to cusp forms must be shown to be regular at the relevant places.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_ordDiff_D_nonneg.lean

